<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n69457" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μυστᾰγωγ-ός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μύστης, ἄγω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>introducing</i> or <i>initiating into
				mysteries,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				IG
				5(1).1390.149
			</span></i> (Andania, <span class="entity">i B.C.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Alc.</u>
				34
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			generally, <i>teacher, guide</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βίου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Men.
					550
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Him.
				<u>Or.</u>
				15.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> in Sicily, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περιηγητής</span>
			, <i>cicerone</i>, esp. at temples, <i><span class="en">
				Cic.
				<u>Verr.</u>
				4.59.132
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>Christian priest</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Men.Prot.
				p.111
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Just.
				<u>Nov.</u>
				137.1
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
